cherrycherrysquarewave-by-funnycurlycatcodefactory for Debian
------------------------------------------------------------

Upstream (fcccf_ccsq_2.zip on scene.org, see debian/copyright) ships the
intro as two self-extracting shell scripts (a dd/gunzip header followed by
the compressed executable):
 - ccsq_original: the original version, with very clippy and distorted audio;
 - ccsq_fixed_audio: the same intro with a softer square wave.
The orig tarball contains ccsq_original as shipped upstream, the
executable extracted from ccsq_fixed_audio, and info.txt. Only the
extracted fixed audio executable is installed.

The executable is linked to libSDL-1.2.so.0, libGL.so.1, libc.so.6 and
libm.so.6. It has no section header table: it must not be stripped, and
dpkg-shlibdeps cannot read it, so the shlibs are computed on a stub (see
debian/rules and debian/shlibs-stub.c) and SDL 1.2 and libGL are declared
by hand in the Depends field of debian/control.

executable seems to be compiled for Lubuntu 18.04 (Ubuntu Bionic), as
stated in info.txt: it was built with Clang and contains no compiler
identification string.

(no output from: strings -a ccsq_fixed_audio | grep -i gcc)

